son" "file_sha256" "7793ca9ea7c44f974e5beda47bcbdd1871701d8f695074cc29af48bc3f5f5f4a"} {"question" "q-163838" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070363/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4309a945f72371e7a242587777f8b50b6ab3b7b25f7720ea0a9f56c7ec316590"} {"question" "q-163838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070363/state.json" "file_sha256" "7793ca9ea7c44f974e5beda47bcbdd1871701d8f695074cc29af48bc3f5f5f4a"} {"question" "q-163838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070363/state.json" "file_sha256" "7793ca9ea7c44f974e5beda47bcbdd1871701d8f695074cc29af48bc3f5f5f4a"} {"question" "q-163838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070363/state.json" "file_sha256" "7793ca9ea7c44f974e5beda47bcbdd1871701d8f695074cc29af48bc3f5f5f4a"} {"question" "q-164164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070363/assets/9bafb9e41a34d03b70ca2b06bbb8c498f12b51f6e1625ddcd3a95fc4edbbccb6.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $z=f(x,y)$ is shown above. Which of the points shown are local minimum points?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070363/state.json" "file_sha256" "7793ca9ea7c44f974e5beda47bcbdd1871701d8f695074cc29af48bc3f5f5f4a"} {"question" "q-164164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A function $f(x,y)$ has a local minimum point at $(a,b)$ if $f(x,y)\\ge f(a,b)$ for all points $(x,y)$ in a neighborhood of $(a,b).$ \n\nIn other words, we can take a neighborhood of $(x,y)$-values such that the point $(x,y,f(x,y))$ is the lowest point on the graph in the neighborhood.\n\nSuch regions exist for the points $B$ and $D.$ Hence, $B$ and $D$ are local minimum points.\n\n**Note**: For the point $D({x}_{D},{y}_{D},{z}_{D}),$ there are points $(x,y)$ in the surrounding regions such that $f({x}_{D},{y}_{D})=f(x,y).$ However, since the definition of local extrema is non-strict, $f(x,y)\\ge f(a,b)$, the point $D$ does satisfy the conditions for a local minimum.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070363/assets/b5e614ba1e002bef688b899e9f837ed3199748f02dd41e822340219b0201c492.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070363/state.json" "file_sha256" "7793ca9ea7c44f974e5beda47bcbdd1871701d8f695074cc29af48bc3f5f5f4a"} {"question" "q-164164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070363/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4309a945f72371e7a242587777f8b50b6ab3b7b25f7720ea0a9f56c7ec316590"} {"question" "q-164164" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070363/state.json" "file_sha256" "7793ca9ea7c44f974e5beda47bcbdd1871701d8f695074cc29af48bc3f5f5f4a"} {"q